 ## Description
 
-The FSRESTModuleImpl provides a REST facade for the file system module. Unlike session-scoped REST facades (e.g., Link), file system operations are not owned by a session, so this module registers a root namespace `/agent/fs` on [RESTModuleImpl](/modules/RESTModuleImpl) via `registerNamespace("fs", this, false)` rather than a session-scoped namespace. All requests under `/agent/fs/*` are delegated to the public methods of [FSModuleImpl](/modules/FSModuleImpl) — the same domain logic used by the SOAP (JAX-WS) endpoint.
+The FSRESTModuleImpl provides a REST facade for the file system module. The SOAP endpoint of [FSModuleImpl](/modules/FSModuleImpl) is published with `requireSession = true`, so this module registers its namespace the same way, `registerNamespace("fs", this, true)` on [RESTModuleImpl](/modules/RESTModuleImpl): the core mounts it under `/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs`, resolves the session token once and delegates every request together with the session, which the file operations do not otherwise use. All requests under `/agent/sessions/{sessionToken}/fs/*` are delegated to the public methods of [FSModuleImpl](/modules/FSModuleImpl) — the same domain logic used by the SOAP (JAX-WS) endpoint.
 
 Paths travel URL-encoded in the `path` query parameter and are interpreted exactly as SOAP interprets them. File payloads use `application/octet-stream` content type.
 
+## Activation
+
+The module is optional. Append it to the module list in `agent.properties`; it loads `FSModuleImpl` automatically:
+
+```properties
+Agent.modules=internal.DiagnosticsModule;core.FSModuleImpl;core.ProcessModuleImpl;core.RESTModuleImpl;core.FSRESTModuleImpl;
+```
+
